message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Every Separable Metric Space Extends to an Extreme One"
abstract: >-
  The bounded-by-one pseudometrics on a set form a compact convex set. For a finite set this
  is a rational polytope, so its extreme points have rational distances and satisfy strong
  rigidity constraints. This paper shows that no such restriction survives passage to an
  infinite set: every separable bounded-by-one pseudometric space is the restriction of an
  extreme point of the metric body of a larger space obtained by adding only countably many
  points. Accompanied by a complete Lean 4 formalization.
type: software
